  "ordinary_scope": "Observed request lengths and verification counts, with one prompt sample plus B1 bonus/T5 verification per round. Sensitivity assumes B1-equivalent rows, full end-to-end exposure, and original response denominators. Random IDs, acceptance, actual batch composition, cache and service latency can change.",
  "branch_decisions": {
    "greedy": "No top-k/top-p work in the bound greedy samples.",
    "no_k_no_p": "Filter returns the original alias. The joint mask removes no work.",
    "k_only_or_p_only": "One cutoff mask. The measured K-only speedup switches from full sort to bounded top-k and has no fusion credit here.",
    "both": "The two comparisons consume the original FP32 probabilities. Apply their union once to the original logits, preserving ties, cutoff and return alias.",
    "raw_or_processed_scores": "Both-cutoff pricing covers only the mask update. Raw readers keep pre-processor logits. Processed logits remain visible if requested. Processed logprobs keep FP32 log_softmax. Internal bonus requests a score plane even with public scores off; the rejection path reads it for requested logprobs.",
    "id_only_or_score_live_random": "A distinct fusion can feed exact FP32 softmax into division by the existing exponential noise and ArgMax. For ordinary/bonus, a sole-consumer probability and divided plane each have 8*B*V logical write/read bytes. RNG order, ties, stream handoff and all score readers remain. No timing credit for this epilogue.",
    "verification": "T rows form one call. Rejection acceptance, possible recovery and entropy can require dense probabilities or original scores. No bonus-only epilogue credit on T rows. Mixed greedy rows retain pre-filter greedy IDs.",
    "batch_invariant": "Ordinary/bonus may delegate to upstream sampling with different tie semantics. Verify the active path before transferring the measured mask delta. Ascend target apply_sampling_constraints imports the Ascend cutoff directly."
